# template: support
# Written by `bifrost-bench suite init -template support`. A support suite
# tests a customer support agent in a conversation (docs/customer-support.md).
# Each task starts two MCP servers from the image built from
# services/helpdesk/: the helpdesk (orders, subscriptions, the support
# policy), seeded with the task's seed/db.json, and the customer, the user
# simulator, driven by the task's user.json (a script and a persona). The
# agent talks to the customer only with respond_to_user and reaches both
# servers through the per-run tool proxy, which records every call in
# tools.jsonl. After the agent exits the helpdesk database and the
# conversation are exported and the hidden verifier (verifier/tests/verify.py
# with the task's checks.py) scores three dimensions: db, policy and
# communicate.
#
# simulator: the user simulator. mode scripted (the default) replays each
# task's script deterministically and calls no model. mode llm has a pinned
# model play the customer from the persona: set provider and model here or in
# an experiment's simulator: block; its calls go through the gateway on the
# simulator's own key and are reported as simulator_cost_usd, apart from the
# agent's cost. Results from an llm user are labelled "simulated user
# (model: X)" and never compared with scripted-user runs.
id: [[.ID]]
version: 0.1.0
description: Customer support conversations graded on the helpdesk's final state, the policy and what the customer was told.
track: support
environment: docker_workspace
grader: verifier_command
base_image:
[[- if .Dockerfile]]
  dockerfile: base/Dockerfile
[[- end]]
  tag: [[.Image]]
workdir: /workspace
output:
  kind: state
simulator:
  mode: scripted
  prompt_version: user-v1
  max_turns: 12
verifier:
  command: ["python3", "/grader/tests/verify.py"]
  result: reward
  result_path: /grader/out/reward.json
  pass_threshold: 1
  restore: []
  timeout_s: 120
tasks: [refund-in-policy]
probes: [model-outage, tool-error-first, hostile-customer]
